--[[
	============================================================================
	ROBLOX REAL-TIME STENCIL SHADOW ENGINE (v19 - True Silhouettes & Light Occlusion)
	============================================================================
	Client-side (LocalScript / StarterPlayerScripts / executor). Draws crisp
	shadows on the surfaces that actually receive the sunlight.

	WHAT'S NEW IN v19
	1. TRUE PLAYER SILHOUETTES (no more "bunch of cylinders"):
	   - Each nearby character is mirrored into a black-lit ViewportFrame that
	     looks down the sun direction. The render is placed on the receiving
	     surface through a light-aligned SurfaceGui whose canvas is stretched by
	     exactly 1/cos(incidence) along the light's slope, which is the exact
	     parallel projection of the character onto that surface.
	   - The silhouette is the character's real geometry: package / Rthro body
	     meshes, heads, hair, hats, accessories, tools and transparent textures.
	   - Far characters (or when the ViewportFrame budget is used up) fall back
	     to projected oriented boxes of every body part and accessory.
	2. SHADOWS STAY ON THE FIRST SURFACE THE LIGHT HITS (nothing behind walls):
	   - Receivers are found by casting rays from every body part along the
	     light. Surfaces hit first become occluders, and their own shadow region
	     is subtracted (exact convex polygon difference) from every surface
	     behind them, so shadows never leak through walls, floors or steps.
	   - Map shadows sample their footprint back towards the sun and get the
	     same occluder subtraction.
	3. WALKING INTO A SHADOW WORKS LIKE A REAL SHADOW:
	   - Every body part / accessory is tested against the sun. Parts that are
	     already in another object's shadow are darkened (Highlight fill) and
	     removed from the character's own silhouette, so your shadow merges into
	     the building/tree shadow instead of stacking a darker copy on top.
	4. LONG RANGE: distance-based canvas LOD, off-screen tile culling,
	   cached primitive state (only changed GUI properties are written) and
	   larger caster/slot budgets let shadows render far further.
	5. REFINED LOOK: feathered 1px edges, rounded polygon corners, sun-elevation
	   fade, softer moon shadows, Terrain receivers and adjustable darkness.

	Override any CONFIG value before running with:
	    getgenv().StencilShadowConfig = { ShadowDarkness = 0.5, ... }
]]

